// Ch14 camp (optional, the night after the escape, on the cut barge; requires ch14_complete). Liss and Rhen. Liss will
// not sleep. Rhen tries to make Tobin's death mean something and she stops him; then she says the cost she wants, and
// Rhen says the true thing. No jokes (pillar 1). Sets ch14_camp_talk.
title: ch14_camp_the_whole_of_him
location: ch14/lacquer_court
---
Rhen [neutral]: Liss. #line:ch14_camp_001
Liss [cold]: Don't. #line:ch14_camp_002
Rhen [neutral]: I wasn't going to say anything. I'll just sit. #line:ch14_camp_003
Liss [grief]: He volunteered. They wanted a groom and he put his hand up so nobody would get picked. That's the whole of him. #line:ch14_camp_004 #long
Rhen [sad]: That's the whole of a lot of people we've met. #line:ch14_camp_005
Liss [angry]: Don't make him a lesson. #line:ch14_camp_006
Rhen [guilty]: Sorry. You're right. #line:ch14_camp_007
Liss [grief]: Here. Hold this. My hands won't stop. #line:ch14_camp_008
Rhen [neutral]: What is it? #line:ch14_camp_009
Liss [sad]: His wick-tool. He lent it to me in the morning. I was going to give it back after. #line:ch14_camp_010
Liss [determined]: When this ends, whatever she does, I want it to cost them. The Order. Not her. Not us. Them. #line:ch14_camp_011
Rhen [sad]: I don't think it gets to choose who it costs. #line:ch14_camp_012
Liss [grief]: I know. I know it doesn't. #line:ch14_camp_013
<<set $ch14_camp_talk = true>>
===
